	"description": [
		"What makes a microscopic sequence of genetic code one of the most powerful forces on Earth? This course explores the fascinating world of viruses, from their elegant morphology to the complex machinery they use to hijack host cells. We will dissect the life cycles of major human pathogens, examining how they spread, evade the immune system, and cause disease. Beyond the biology of infection, we will discuss the development of vaccines, the rise of emerging global threats, and the cutting-edge use of viruses as tools for gene therapy. Prerequisite: BIO 150; recommended: BIO 227, BIO 231, or BIO 233."
	],
